Package: feedlab
Version: @VERSION@
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Ivan De Cesaris IZ0JNY <ivan@iz0jny.it>
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), xdg-utils
Recommends: gir1.2-webkit2-4.1, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, libgirepository-1.0-1, libcairo2, libcairo-gobject2
Homepage: https://github.com/IZ0JNY/FeedLab
Description: design and simulate microwave dish feeds (10-134 GHz, EME)
 FeedLab designs and simulates feeds/illuminators for microwave dishes from
 10 to 134 GHz (W1GHZ, OE2IGL and classic theory): W2IMU, dual-mode,
 corrugated, VE4MA, Cassegrain sub-reflectors, mode-matching S11, aperture
 efficiency, G/T, mechanical PDF drawings and STEP/STL models, optional
 openEMS full-wave analysis.
 .
 Self-contained: ships its own Python and libraries in /opt/feedlab.
 The app opens in its own window (GTK/WebKit) or in the default browser.
